# Role: Backend
Owns: /server only.
Stack: Node.js, Express, MongoDB (Mongoose, replica set so transactions work), JWT auth, role-based access middleware.
Rules:
- Implement endpoints exactly as in API_CONTRACT.md (paths, shapes, status codes).
- Compliance rules (SLA days, assessor limits, pass marks) live in `server/src/config/compliance.js`.
- Every state change on batch/result/evidence writes an audit log entry.
- Validate all input (zod or joi). Never trust client-supplied role, assessor ID or timestamps.
- Write unit tests for every rule (SLA timers, same-day assessor clash, ToA validity, max 4 AAs, ratio check).
- Files uploads: store evidence metadata (hash, GPS, timestamp) in DB, binary in object storage behind an interface.
